      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0ea00ebe_fa90335c",
        "filename": "org.eclipse.jgit/src/org/eclipse/jgit/transport/PromisorRemoteConfig.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1020855
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-12T18:42:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1. By the code itself it is no clear what encoding is trying to support. \n\nI don\u0027t think we do this with any other line in the protocol (?). If so, we can assume it is valid  ascii here. If it is a problem, we can fix encoding for the whole incoming request in following CLs.",
      "parentUuid": "f8ce2405_1213c9ba",
      "revId": "38f68214a7f37f0f6f1596c0ffa503f735367cb0",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "33d58ba4_2de4d602",
        "filename": "org.eclipse.jgit/src/org/eclipse/jgit/transport/PromisorRemoteConfig.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1022030
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-13T01:41:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Seems like jgit should already have something that does this?\n\nReplaced the custom encoder with `HttpSupport.urlEncode(value, false).replace(\"+\", \"%20\")`.\n\n\u003e By the code itself it is no clear what encoding is trying to support. I don\u0027t think we do this with any other line in the protocol (?)\n\nThis is escaping of `promisor-remote` field values, not validation of the whole incoming request. Git\u0027s [gitprotocol-v2](https://git-scm.com/docs/gitprotocol-v2#_promisor_remotepr_info) requires URL-encoded values, including escaping `,` and `;` even for ASCII input. `HttpSupport.urlEncode()` supplies UTF-8 encoding. We need the additional `.replace()` to convert form-encoded spaces to `%20` because the protocol decoder treats `+` literally. Literal plus signs are encoded as `%2B`.\n\n`HttpSupport.urlEncode()` produces more escapes than native Git, but preserves the decoded values and meets the protocol requirements, so I think it\u0027s ok.\n\nDoes this seem better?",
      "parentUuid": "0ea00ebe_fa90335c",
      "revId": "38f68214a7f37f0f6f1596c0ffa503f735367cb0",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a6aa72a_f5d715cb",
        "filename": "org.eclipse.jgit/src/org/eclipse/jgit/transport/PromisorRemoteConfig.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1020855
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-13T20:35:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is much clearer, thanks!\n\nI guess most of the incoming request is fixed strings (or sha1s), not so much content that needs to encode special characters.",
      "parentUuid": "33d58ba4_2de4d602",
      "revId": "38f68214a7f37f0f6f1596c0ffa503f735367cb0",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
